Hint.Settings.CloudUse=This one turns on and off your use of cloud voices, meaning all the voices from the Internet, not your installed SAPI or One Core voices.\n\nIt decides whether those voices are OFFERED when you choose a voice for a particular book. They are never assigned automatically and never become a language's default voice — that stays with the voices installed on this computer, which cost nothing and need no connection.\n\nA book already reading with a cloud voice keeps it whether this is on or off; the switch governs the picker, not what can be played.
Hint.Settings.Azure=The use of Google and Azure voices requires some Google, Microsoft and Azure credentials and a bit of work on their web. Read more in Help.
Hint.Settings.Cloud=
Google.Cred.NotJson=That file is not readable as JSON, so it is not the one Google gave you. The file you want was downloaded when you created the service account, and its name ends in .json.
Google.Cred.NotServiceAccount=That JSON is readable but it is not a service account — it has no account address and no private key in it. Google offers several kinds of credential; the one for these voices is the service account key.

