Dialog.About.Text=Nemoviz Book Reader {0}\n\nBuild of {1}\n\nThis is a multiformat and multioutput reader for digital books and publications, specially designed for the blind, visually impaired and people with reading disabilities. It is free for basic usage, but if you want to explore and use its advanced features such as translation and cloud voices you will need to register and possibly pay for the respective external services.\n\nMade by Nemoguća vizija — nemoviz.org\n\nWritten by Gordan Radić\n\nBuilt with Claude (Anthropic). Much of the code was written by it, to the author's design, decisions and measurements; the copyright and the licence are his.\n\n{2}\n\nWHAT NBR IS BUILT ON\n\nNBR plays sound through libmpv, reads braille through liblouis, speaks through the NVDA controller client, reads tags with TagLib#, takes text out of PDFs with PdfPig, and opens archives with SharpCompress. Each is a separate library, used unmodified, and each can be replaced by a compatible build of its own.\n\nlibmpv, and the FFmpeg inside it — LGPL 2.1 or later\n\nliblouis and its braille tables — LGPL 2.1 or later\n\nNVDA Controller Client — LGPL 2.1\n\nTagLib# — LGPL 2.1\n\nPdfPig — Apache License 2.0\n\nSharpCompress and the Microsoft packages — MIT\n\nAndika, Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, Lexend and OpenDyslexic — SIL Open Font License 1.1\n\nLuciole — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0\n\nThe full notice — versions, copyright holders, and where each licence was read from — is in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt beside the program, and the licence texts themselves are in the Licences folder.
